---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Accessibility"
  description="Keyboard, no-JavaScript, text zoom, and reduced-motion guidance for The True Hive, with the accessibility target and verification limits explained."
>
  <section class="page-intro wrap" aria-labelledby="accessibility-title">
    <p class="eyebrow">Make yourself at home</p>
    <h1 id="accessibility-title">
      Accessibility,
      <br />
      <em>at your pace.</em>
    </h1>
    <p>
      WCAG 2.2 AA is the target for this website. This guidance is not a
      certification or a promise of universal accessibility across every
      browser, device, and assistive technology.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="wrap prose-section">
    <h2>Getting around with a keyboard</h2>
    <p>
      Use Tab to move forward through links and controls, and Shift + Tab to
      move back. The first link, “Skip to content,” takes you past the shared
      navigation to the main content when activated with Enter.
    </p>
    <p>
      Collection filters use native controls: choose a category with the arrow
      keys, type in the search field, then activate the “Find goods” button with
      Enter or Space. Links and buttons have visible focus styles to help you
      keep your place.
    </p>
    <h2>Browse without JavaScript</h2>
    <p>
      The public collection, category filters, search, and page navigation work
      without JavaScript. Choose a collection, optionally enter search terms,
      and select “Find goods” to load the results. Use “Clear filters” when it
      appears, or return to the collection to start again.
    </p>
    <a class="text-link" href="/goods">
      Browse the collection <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
    </a>
    <h2>Text size and reduced motion</h2>
    <p>
      Use your browser's text-size or zoom controls to make the content more
      comfortable to read. Pages are designed to reflow as the available width
      changes rather than requiring a fixed screen size.
    </p>
    <p>
      Your device's reduced-motion preference limits the site's optional
      transitions. No animation is needed to read the collection or use its
      navigation.
    </p>
    <h2>Read the words alongside the artwork</h2>
    <p>
      The site's original illustrations are not product or farm photographs.
      Read the adjacent descriptions and concept or planning labels for what is
      actually confirmed. An illustration is not evidence of availability or a
      service commitment.
    </p>
    <h2>What checks can and cannot tell us</h2>
    <p>
      Automated checks can flag some accessibility issues, but cannot prove a
      site is usable for everyone. Local automated checks and limited keyboard
      and layout inspection do not replace manual review with real screen
      readers and assistive devices.
    </p>
    <p>
      That real-world review remains necessary. No completed assistive-device
      audit, independent endorsement, or certified screen-reader review is
      claimed here.
    </p>
    <h2>If something gets in your way</h2>
    <p>
      Check the existing contact channels for confirmed phone or profile links.
      Those channels may still be pending. This page does not submit feedback or
      send a message, and it does not provide a response-time commitment.
    </p>
    <a class="text-link" href="/#connect">
      Check contact channels <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
    </a>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
